                      (    forth6809.asm):05433         ; TSTCOMPARE - comparison tests (glossary section 3.7). Covers
                      (    forth6809.asm):05434         ; every word in that section. Like several words in the previous
                      (    forth6809.asm):05435         ; group, most of these modify the top of stack in place rather
                      (    forth6809.asm):05436         ; than PULU/PSHU - the tests verify what's observable via the
                      (    forth6809.asm):05437         ; stack either way. Signed vs unsigned comparisons (</U<, >/U>)
                      (    forth6809.asm):05438         ; each tested with a case that would give the opposite answer
                      (    forth6809.asm):05439         ; under the other convention, confirming genuine sign-awareness
                      (    forth6809.asm):05440         ; rather than an accidentally-shared implementation. WITHIN
                      (    forth6809.asm):05441         ; tested against a wraparound range specifically (n2 near $FFFF,
                      (    forth6809.asm):05442         ; n3 wrapped past $0000), both inside and outside cases - the
                      (    forth6809.asm):05443         ; documented special case its own unsigned-offset implementation
                      (    forth6809.asm):05444         ; exists to handle, not just an ordinary non-wrapping range. D</
                      (    forth6809.asm):05445         ; DU< both tested with equal high cells and different low cells -
                      (    forth6809.asm):05446         ; the documented tie-break case a naive high-cell-only comparison
                      (    forth6809.asm):05447         ; would get wrong.
                      (    forth6809.asm):05448         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
