                      (    forth6809.asm):06238         ; Control-flow test harness (glossary section 3.8). Each test
                      (    forth6809.asm):06239         ; redirects CODEHERE to a scratch buffer (TSTCBUF), calls the
                      (    forth6809.asm):06240         ; real compile-time control-flow words directly (JSR IF, JSR
                      (    forth6809.asm):06241         ; THEN, etc - the same routines the compiler itself calls when
                      (    forth6809.asm):06242         ; parsing IF/THEN/DO/LOOP/etc, not a hand-simulated imitation),
                      (    forth6809.asm):06243         ; then restores CODEHERE and executes the compiled snippet
                      (    forth6809.asm):06244         ; directly. This tests the actual interaction between compile-
                      (    forth6809.asm):06245         ; time correctness (right bytes, right patched offsets) and
                      (    forth6809.asm):06246         ; runtime correctness (right control flow) in one coherent
                      (    forth6809.asm):06247         ; test, without needing the outer interpreter, FIND, or a
                      (    forth6809.asm):06248         ; dictionary entry - matching the ANS test suite's own planned
                      (    forth6809.asm):06249         ; role for broader standards-compliance coverage; these tests
                      (    forth6809.asm):06250         ; specifically verify this system's own compile/patch mechanism
                      (    forth6809.asm):06251         ; works correctly, not full end-to-end parsing.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06252         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):06253         
                      (    forth6809.asm):06254         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):06255         ; TSTIFT1 - unit test for IF/THEN, true case. Compiles
                      (    forth6809.asm):06256         ; "IF <lit 111> THEN" into scratch, then runs it with a true
                      (    forth6809.asm):06257         ; flag - the branch is NOT taken, so 111 should be pushed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06258         ; Verified by hand-trace before writing: ZBRANCH's patched
                      (    forth6809.asm):06259         ; offset comes out to 7 (from the placeholder field to just
                      (    forth6809.asm):06260         ; past the compiled LIT+111), correctly skipping nothing when
                      (    forth6809.asm):06261         ; the flag is true and falling through into the literal.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06262         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
C239                  (    forth6809.asm):06263         TSTIFT1: LDD   CODEHERE
                      (    forth6809.asm):06264                  STD   TSTCSAV
                      (    forth6809.asm):06265                  LDD   #TSTCBUF
                      (    forth6809.asm):06266                  STD   CODEHERE
