                      (    forth6809.asm):06688         ; TSTRECUR - unit test for RECURSE. Builds a fake dictionary
                      (    forth6809.asm):06689         ; header in scratch (TSTFHDR: LEN/FL=3, name "FOO", a
                      (    forth6809.asm):06690         ; don't-care LINK, and DUP's real address as the CFA), points
                      (    forth6809.asm):06691         ; LATEST at it, then calls RECURSE directly. Verifies RECURSE
                      (    forth6809.asm):06692         ; correctly parses an arbitrary header (LEN/FL's 5-bit length
                      (    forth6809.asm):06693         ; field, skipping name+LINK to reach the CFA) and compiles a
                      (    forth6809.asm):06694         ; correct call to it - tests the actual mechanism (header
                      (    forth6809.asm):06695         ; parsing, CFA extraction, CCALL), not genuine self-recursion,
                      (    forth6809.asm):06696         ; which would need a real in-progress compilation to set up
                      (    forth6809.asm):06697         ; meaningfully. Confirmed by hand-trace: RECURSE's own address
                      (    forth6809.asm):06698         ; arithmetic (+1 past LEN/FL, +namelen past the name, +2 past
                      (    forth6809.asm):06699         ; LINK) lands exactly on TSTFHDR+6, where the CFA is placed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):06700         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
