                      (    forth6809.asm):07751         ; TSTDEFWORDS - defining-words tests (glossary section 3.9, 17
                      (    forth6809.asm):07752         ; words, 12 tests since VALUE/TO and IS/ACTION-OF are each
                      (    forth6809.asm):07753         ; combined into one test). Every defining word parses a name
                      (    forth6809.asm):07754         ; from the input source via WORD (HEADER's own mechanism,
                      (    forth6809.asm):07755         ; shared by :/CREATE) - a complexity nothing in section 3.8 had.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07756         ; Each test redirects CODEHERE, DPHERE, VARHERE, and
                      (    forth6809.asm):07757         ; SRCADDR/SRCLEN/TOIN together (a fake name, "TESTWD", reused
                      (    forth6809.asm):07758         ; safely across every test here since each redirect/restore
                      (    forth6809.asm):07759         ; cycle is fully isolated), calls the real defining word
                      (    forth6809.asm):07760         ; directly, saves the newly-defined word's own CFA (= CODEHERE
                      (    forth6809.asm):07761         ; at the moment the defining word was called), restores
                      (    forth6809.asm):07762         ; everything, then executes that CFA directly to verify runtime
                      (    forth6809.asm):07763         ; behavior.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07764         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07765         ; A real, structurally important finding from this section:
                      (    forth6809.asm):07766         ; HEADER writes to the real LATEST variable unconditionally, not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07767         ; a redirectable copy like CODEHERE/DPHERE/VARHERE - every test
                      (    forth6809.asm):07768         ; here explicitly saves and restores it, confirmed necessary by
                      (    forth6809.asm):07769         ; reading HEADER's own code directly, not assumed safe by analogy
                      (    forth6809.asm):07770         ; with the other three pointers.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07771         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07772         ; MARKER's own test is the one exception to the general
                      (    forth6809.asm):07773         ; redirect-then-restore-then-execute order: DOMARKER (confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):07774         ; by reading it directly) writes to the real DPHERE/CODEHERE/
                      (    forth6809.asm):07775         ; VARHERE/LATEST unconditionally too, so that test executes the
                      (    forth6809.asm):07776         ; marker word while still redirected, only restoring the real
                      (    forth6809.asm):07777         ; environment afterward - getting this order backwards would
                      (    forth6809.asm):07778         ; have corrupted the real dictionary pointers with scratch
                      (    forth6809.asm):07779         ; addresses.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07780         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):07781         ; Bare CREATE (never followed by DOES>) is deliberately not
                      (    forth6809.asm):07782         ; tested on its own - traced its placeholder "behavior field"
                      (    forth6809.asm):07783         ; (a genuine compiled JSR DOESRT0 instruction) and confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):07784         ; DODOES reads that field as raw data, not as code to execute -
                      (    forth6809.asm):07785         ; which only produces a valid jump target for the raw-address
                      (    forth6809.asm):07786         ; form every other defining word uses (VARIABLE, CONSTANT, etc,
                      (    forth6809.asm):07787         ; via CODECOMMA), not CREATE's own placeholder JSR instruction.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07788         ; Bare CREATE's own direct-execution behavior isn't meant to be
                      (    forth6809.asm):07789         ; relied upon before a DOES> patches it.
                      (    forth6809.asm):07790         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
C239 BDFC2B           (    forth6809.asm):07791         TSTDEFWORDS: JSR CRW
C23C 8EC24D           (    forth6809.asm):07792                    LDX   #TSTDEFMSG
C23F 3610             (    forth6809.asm):07793                    PSHU  X
