                      (    forth6809.asm):09539         ; Compiling-words test harness (glossary section 3.10). Reuses
                      (    forth6809.asm):09540         ; the scratch infrastructure established for sections 3.8/3.9
                      (    forth6809.asm):09541         ; (TSTCBUF/TSTCBUF2 for CODEHERE redirects, TSTFHDR for a fake
                      (    forth6809.asm):09542         ; dictionary header, TSTNAMEB for a fake source name). POSTPONE
                      (    forth6809.asm):09543         ; is this section's own hardest case: a genuine two-level
                      (    forth6809.asm):09544         ; compile-time mechanism (compiling code that, for a normal
                      (    forth6809.asm):09545         ; word, itself compiles a call to that word later, when the
                      (    forth6809.asm):09546         ; current definition eventually runs - not immediately, unlike
                      (    forth6809.asm):09547         ; every other compile-time word tested so far). ABORT" is safely
                      (    forth6809.asm):09548         ; testable for both its true and false flag cases - traced its
                      (    forth6809.asm):09549         ; own runtime behavior directly and confirmed it uses THROW -2
                      (    forth6809.asm):09550         ; internally, not the raw, never-returns ABORT mechanism plain
                      (    forth6809.asm):09551         ; ABORT itself uses (which remains untested, per section 3.1's
                      (    forth6809.asm):09552         ; own reasoning).
