                      (    forth6809.asm):10215         ; TSTPOSTPONE1 - unit test for POSTPONE, normal (non-immediate)
                      (    forth6809.asm):10216         ; word case. Traced its own code first: for a normal word,
                      (    forth6809.asm):10217         ; POSTPONE compiles "[LIT xt][JSR COMPILE,]" into the current
                      (    forth6809.asm):10218         ; definition - NOT a direct call to the word itself. This is
                      (    forth6809.asm):10219         ; standard ANS semantics (POSTPONE appends a word's own
                      (    forth6809.asm):10220         ; compilation semantics to the current definition; for an
                      (    forth6809.asm):10221         ; ordinary word, that semantics IS "compile a call to it", so
                      (    forth6809.asm):10222         ; the current definition, when it later runs, must itself
                      (    forth6809.asm):10223         ; perform that compiling action against whatever definition is
                      (    forth6809.asm):10224         ; being compiled at that later point - not immediately). Given
                      (    forth6809.asm):10225         ; the genuine complexity of fully executing that second level
                      (    forth6809.asm):10226         ; (which would need a further redirected CODEHERE and a further
                      (    forth6809.asm):10227         ; round of execute-and-verify), this test instead verifies the
                      (    forth6809.asm):10228         ; compiled byte sequence directly - still a meaningful,
                      (    forth6809.asm):10229         ; unambiguous check of POSTPONE's own documented mechanism.
                      (    forth6809.asm):10230         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
