                      (    forth6809.asm):10342         ; TSTPOSTPONE2 - unit test for POSTPONE, immediate word case.
                      (    forth6809.asm):10343         ; Confirmed via FIND's own code that it pushes 1 for immediate
                      (    forth6809.asm):10344         ; words, -1 otherwise - POSTPONEW branches on exactly that. For
                      (    forth6809.asm):10345         ; an immediate word, its own "compilation semantics" IS
                      (    forth6809.asm):10346         ; "execute it now" (that's what immediate means), so POSTPONE
                      (    forth6809.asm):10347         ; compiles a direct call to it - simpler to verify than the
                      (    forth6809.asm):10348         ; normal-word case, no second level involved.
                      (    forth6809.asm):10349         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
