                      (    forth6809.asm):12423         ; to verify PARSE's own documented distinguishing behavior -
                      (    forth6809.asm):12424         ; "does not skip leading delimiters, unlike WORD" - the leading
                      (    forth6809.asm):12425         ; comma should be hit immediately, returning a zero-length token
                      (    forth6809.asm):12426         ; right where TOIN started, not skipped over to find "XY".
