                      (    forth6809.asm):19025                                  ; (same class as TRYNUM/STOD/SIGN's own fixes
                      (    forth6809.asm):19026                                  ; elsewhere in this file), so BPL was always
                      (    forth6809.asm):19027                                  ; testing CLR's result, not n1's actual sign.
                      (    forth6809.asm):19028                                  ; BPL always branched, meaning n1 was NEVER
                      (    forth6809.asm):19029                                  ; negated even when genuinely negative - found
                      (    forth6809.asm):19030                                  ; via MAME: TSTMSTAR's two returned values
                      (    forth6809.asm):19031                                  ; came back wrong, which turned out to be
                      (    forth6809.asm):19032                                  ; this, not a push-order swap in the test
                      (    forth6809.asm):19033                                  ; itself. FMSLASHMOD/SMSLASHREM already do
                      (    forth6809.asm):19034                                  ; this correctly (explicit TST PRODHI between
                      (    forth6809.asm):19035                                  ; their own CLR calls and the branch) - MSTAR
                      (    forth6809.asm):19036                                  ; was simply missing the equivalent re-test.
