                      (    forth6809.asm):20880         ; ENVIRONMENT? - dispatcher complete; table has entries derived
                      (    forth6809.asm):20881         ; without fabricating unfixed capacities. /HOLD and /PAD were both
                      (    forth6809.asm):20882         ; added this session, answering HOLDMINSIZE and PADMINSIZE
                      (    forth6809.asm):20883         ; respectively (see each entry itself, below, for why each uses its
                      (    forth6809.asm):20884         ; own, conceptually correct constant rather than the numerically-
                      (    forth6809.asm):20885         ; equal PADOFFSET).
                      (    forth6809.asm):20886         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):20887         ; WORDLISTS (16.3.2, Search-Order word set) is deliberately absent
                      (    forth6809.asm):20888         ; from ENVTABLE, not an oversight - this system doesn't implement
                      (    forth6809.asm):20889         ; the Search-Order word set, so WORDLISTS is genuinely an unknown
                      (    forth6809.asm):20890         ; attribute here. Per ENVIRONMENT?'s own spec (6.1.1345): "If the
                      (    forth6809.asm):20891         ; system treats the attribute as unknown, the returned flag is
                      (    forth6809.asm):20892         ; false" - falling through to ENVNOTFOUND already produces exactly
                      (    forth6809.asm):20893         ; that, correctly and completely, with no dispatcher work needed.
                      (    forth6809.asm):20894         ; Confirmed via MAME testing.
                      (    forth6809.asm):20895         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):20896         ; MAX-D/MAX-UD were resolved this session via a genuine dispatcher
                      (    forth6809.asm):20897         ; extension, not just a table entry - both are double-cell values
                      (    forth6809.asm):20898         ; per their own ANS data type, which the original single-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):20899         ; ENVFOUND (pushing exactly one value before TRUE) couldn't
                      (    forth6809.asm):20900         ; represent. Added a second table (ENVTABLE2) and matching loop
                      (    forth6809.asm):20901         ; (ENV2START/ENV2LOOP/ENV2FOUND, below) specifically for double-cell
                      (    forth6809.asm):20902         ; entries, rather than reworking the single-cell path to handle both
                      (    forth6809.asm):20903         ; shapes - see those labels for the full design.
                      (    forth6809.asm):20904         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):20905         ; FLOORED was the third, separate open item flagged previously -
                      (    forth6809.asm):20906         ; investigated this session by tracing DIVCOMMON (shared by /, MOD,
                      (    forth6809.asm):20907         ; /MOD) against this system's own SM/REM and FM/MOD. Confirmed
                      (    forth6809.asm):20908         ; DIVCOMMON matches SM/REM's convention exactly (remainder sign
